<section class="page-intro shell">
  <p class="eyebrow">Privacy policy</p><h1>Your styles stay yours.</h1>
  <div class="page-lede"><p>StylePort has no advertising, cross-app tracking, behavioral analytics, or account system. Your styles and browsing history stay out of its optional purchase reporting.</p><p class="policy-date">Effective October 7, 2026</p></div>
</section>
<article class="prose shell">
  <section><h2>Data stored on your device</h2><p>StylePort stores the styles you import or create, their settings, and extension preferences in Safari’s extension storage on your Mac. This information stays on your device unless you choose to export a backup or otherwise share it.</p><p>Removing styles deletes them from StylePort. Removing the app and its extension causes macOS and Safari to control deletion of the remaining local app data.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Website access</h2><p>Safari website access is required so StylePort can determine which user-selected styles match a page and apply their compiled CSS. StylePort does not use this access to build or transmit browsing history.</p><p>You control website access in Safari Settings and can restrict or revoke it at any time. Revoking access prevents StylePort from styling those websites.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Network requests you initiate</h2><p>StylePort can retrieve a style when you provide its URL and can check an installed style’s update URL when you request or enable updates. Those requests go to the host named by the style or URL. That host may receive ordinary network information such as your IP address and user agent under its own privacy policy.</p><p>The Safari release does not inject marketplace installation hooks and does not provide cloud synchronization.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Optional in-app tips</h2><p>The App Store and TestFlight builds offer optional, one-time tips through Apple’s In-App Purchase system and RevenueCat. Tips do not unlock features and are not subscriptions. Every StylePort feature remains free.</p><p>RevenueCat is initialized only when you open the native tip jar, not during ordinary styling. It processes an anonymous app user identifier, purchase records, and related product, currency, and app information to validate purchases and provide purchase reporting. StylePort does not provide RevenueCat with your name, email address, styles, or browsing history, and does not enable advertising identifier collection. Apple handles payment information; StylePort and RevenueCat do not receive your card details.</p><p>Deleting local app data does not itself delete purchase records held by Apple or RevenueCat. Their handling and retention of that information are governed by the <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy/">RevenueCat Privacy Policy</a>.</p></section>
  <section><h2>App data collection declaration</h2><p>StylePort’s Apple privacy manifest declares purchase history used for app functionality and purchase analytics. It declares that this data is not linked to you and is not used for tracking. The manifest declares no tracking and no tracking domains.</p><p>StylePort does not track you across other companies’ apps or websites for advertising. Its optional purchase reporting does not include your styles, browsing history, name, email address, or card details and does not create a StylePort account.</p></section>
  <section><h2>This website</h2><p>The StylePort website does not use advertising trackers, analytics scripts, or marketing cookies. Its appearance follows your device by default. If you choose Light or Dark, the website saves only that preference in your browser under <code>styleport-appearance</code>; choosing System removes it.</p><p>The website does not currently operate a waitlist or email signup form. If you email support, your email provider and RelayByte’s email provider process the message and address you choose to send.</p><p>GitHub may process ordinary request information needed to deliver and protect the site, such as an IP address, request time, and browser details, under GitHub’s own terms.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Optional website support</h2><p>The “Support StylePort” button on this website opens a Stripe-hosted checkout operated for RelayByte. This website payment is separate from the native app’s Apple and RevenueCat tip jar. Stripe processes the email address, payment and billing information, transaction details, and fraud-prevention data needed to complete the payment. The StylePort website does not receive your full card details.</p><p>RelayByte receives the payment record Stripe makes available, including the amount, email address, payment status, and related transaction information. Stripe handles checkout data under its <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy">privacy policy</a>. Support is voluntary, is not a charitable donation, and does not purchase a license or unlock product features.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Changes and contact</h2><p>Material changes will be reflected by a new effective date. For privacy questions or requests, email <a href="mailto:{{ site.supportEmail }}">{{ site.supportEmail }}</a>.</p></section>
</article>
